<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav March wages rise 2.6 pct to 713 dinars.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav March wages rise 2.6 pct to 713 dinars.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV AVERAGE NET WAGES   MAR 97     FEB 97     MAR 96</p>
<p> wage in dinars		     713	  695	  546</p>
<p> month/month pct change	  +2.6	+12.5	 +4.4</p>
<p>NOTES -- Under a new methodology of calculating average wages introduced in January 1997, data include all employed who worked in a given month, regardless of whether they all received wages earned in that month.</p>
<p>Data do not include private sector. Data cover rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
